seph Pulitzer were involved in a circulation war, with Hearst using sensationalist journalism to
{'id': 5225, 'user': 'Who is the child of the musician who wrote the lyrics to The Sound of Silence?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The original question asks for the child of the musician who wrote the lyrics to "The Sound of Silence." To answer this, I first need to identify who wrote the lyrics to the song, as that is the starting point in determining the parent of the child in question.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Who wrote the lyrics to The Sound of Silence?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "``The Sound of Silence'', originally ``The Sounds of Silence'', is a song by the American music duo Simon & Garfunkel. The song was written by Paul Simon over a period of several months in 1963 and 1964. A studio audition led to the duo signing a record deal with Columbia Records, and the song was recorded in March 1964 at Columbia Studios in New York City for inclusion on their debut album, Wednesday Morning, 3 A.M..", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context states that "The Sound of Silence" was written by Paul Simon over several months in 1963 and 1964. Therefore, the answer is Paul Simon.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Paul Simon', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the child of the musician who wrote the lyrics to "The Sound of Silence." Since Paul Simon is the songwriter of that song, the next step is to determine who his child is, which directly addresses the original question.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Who is the child of Paul Simon?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "It featured Harper Simon, Paul Simon's son. Also, its drummer was Seb Rochford, who won the BBC Rising Star Jazz Award in 2004 and leads the Mercury Prize-nominated experimental-jazz group Polar Bear.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', "The context mentions that Harper Simon is Paul Simon's son. Therefore, the answer is directly provided in the text.", '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Harper Simon', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To determine the answer, first identify the lyricist of "The Sound of Silence," which is Paul Simon. Then, find out who is the child of Paul Simon, which is Harper Simon. Therefore, the final answer is Harper Simon.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'Harper Simon', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 15029, 'user': 'What country is in the middle of the ocean which is next to the county where the McKenzie Bridge is located?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'Now that I know the location of McKenzie Bridge, the next step is to identify the administrative territorial entity it belongs to, which will help determine the country that is in the middle of the ocean and adjacent to that entity.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'In which administrative territorial entity is McKenzie Bridge located?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'McKenzie Bridge is an unincorporated community in Lane County, Oregon, United States, on the McKenzie River and within Willamette National Forest. It is along Oregon Route 126, about east of Eugene, between Rainbow and Belknap Springs. The McKenzie Bridge State Airport is about east of the community.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'To determine the administrative territorial entity where McKenzie Bridge is located, we examine the context provided. The context states that McKenzie Bridge is an unincorporated community in Lane County, Oregon. Since Lane County is a county within the state of Oregon, the answer is clearly identified as Lane County.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Lane County', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To answer the original question, I first need to determine which body of water is adjacent to the county where McKenzie Bridge is located. This information will help identify the country that lies in the middle of that body of water.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Which body of water is next to the county where McKenzie Bridge is located?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Heceta Head ( ) is a headland that stands above the Pacific Ocean in Lane County, Oregon, United States. The Heceta Head Light is located on its south side. Heceta Head is named after the Basque explorer under Spanish Commission, Bruno de Heceta, who explored the Pacific Northwest in the 1770s. The headland marks the end of a lower-lying stretch of the coastline to the south dominated by sand dunes; the coastline to the north is more varied. Devils Elbow is the bay south of the headland at the mouth of Cape Creek, and with the headland formed Devils Elbow State Park, which is now part of Heceta Head Lighthouse State Scenic Viewpoint.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', '\nThe context states that Heceta Head is a headland that stands above the Pacific Ocean in Lane County, Oregon. Since McKenzie Bridge is located in Lane County, the body of water next to it is the Pacific Ocean. Therefore, the answer is Pacific Ocean.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Pacific Ocean', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks for a country that is in the middle of the ocean and is next to the county where the McKenzie Bridge is located. To begin answering this, I first need to identify which country lies in the middle of the Pacific Ocean, as this is a key piece of information required to determine if it meets the condition of being next to the relevant county.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Which country is in the middle of the Pacific Ocean?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'This ocean has most of the islands in the world. There are about 25,000 islands in the Pacific Ocean. The islands entirely within the Pacific Ocean can be divided into three main groups known as Micronesia, Melanesia and Polynesia. Micronesia, which lies north of the equator and west of the International Date Line, includes the Mariana Islands in the northwest, the Caroline Islands in the center, the Marshall Islands to the west and the islands of Kiribati in the southeast.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'the context states that the Pacific Ocean contains three main groups of islands: Micronesia, Melanesia, and Polynesia. It specifically mentions that Micronesia includes the Caroline Islands in the center. Since the question asks for the country (or group) located in the middle of the Pacific Ocean, the answer refers to the Caroline Islands as they are described as being in the center of Micronesia, which is within the Pacific Ocean.', '
{'id': 7554, 'user': 'The mosaic in the church in the place where Baildsa formed is known as what?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The original question asks for the name of the mosaic in the church located in the place where Baildsa formed. To identify which church and mosaic are being referred to, I first need to determine the location where Baildsa formed. This sub-question is the first step in the reasoning chain and is essential for locating the specific church and mosaic mentioned in the original question.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Where was Baildsa formed?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Baildsa is a band from Thessaloniki, Greece. Founded in 2007, the band performs gypsy punk, reggae and ska together with balkan elements. Baildsa\'s sound includes vocals, guitar, bass guitar, drums as well as trumpets and accordion. They have so far toured in Greece, Bulgaria, Albania, and Turkey. Their first album, "United States of Balkans", was released in October 2011, and can be downloaded for free from the band\'s website. Baildsa are currently recording their second album, which is going to be announced in the beginning of 2014. Georgia Myridakis of fridge.gr comments on Baildsa\'s eclectic sound - "Elements, influences and sounds, not lined up in a row, but assembled one by one and all joined together, creating an enthusiastic and very entertaining music.\'', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'the answer is formed by identifying the location mentioned in the context. The context states that "Baildsa is a band from Thessaloniki, Greece," which directly answers the question of where the band was formed. Therefore, the answer is Thessaloniki.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Thessaloniki', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks for the name of the mosaic in the church in the place where Baildsa formed. To address this, I first need to identify the specific location referred to by "the place where Baildsa formed," which is likely Thessaloniki. Therefore, the sub-question is asked to establish the connection between Baildsa and Thessaloniki, and to focus the search on the mosaic in the church there.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'What is the name of the mosaic in the church in Thessaloniki?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "Very few early Byzantine mosaics survived the Iconoclastic destruction of the 8th century. Among the rare examples are the 6th-century Christ in majesty (or Ezekiel's Vision) mosaic in the apse of the Church of Hosios David in Thessaloniki that was hidden behind mortar during those dangerous times. Nine mosaic panels in the Hagios Demetrios Church, which were made between 634 and 730, also escaped destruction. Unusually almost all represent Saint Demetrios of Thessaloniki, often with suppliants before him.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', "The context mentions that the 6th-century Christ in majesty (or Ezekiel's Vision) mosaic is located in the apse of the Church of Hosios David in Thessaloniki. This directly answers the question by identifying the name of the mosaic in the church in Thessaloniki.", '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', "Christ in majesty (or Ezekiel's Vision)", '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks for the name of the mosaic in the church in the place where Baildsa formed. First, we determine where Baildsa formed, which is Thessaloniki. Next, we find the name of the mosaic in the church located in Thessaloniki, which is "Christ in majesty (or Ezekiel\'s Vision)." Therefore, the final answer is "Christ in majesty (or Ezekiel\'s Vision).', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', "Christ in majesty (or Ezekiel's Vision)", '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 19660, 'user': 'What airport sharing a state with KOFI is the busiest?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'To answer the original question about the busiest airport that shares a state with KOFI, I first need to determine which state KOFI is located in. This is the foundational step, as it will allow me to identify airports in that state and then evaluate which one is the busiest.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'In which state is KOFI located?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'KOFI (1180 AM) is a radio station licensed to serve Kalispell, Montana. The station is owned by KOFI, Inc. It airs an Oldies music and News/Talk radio format. The station first signed on in 1955. It was assigned these call letters by the Federal Communications Commission.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The answer is formed by identifying the location mentioned in the context. The context states that KOFI is a radio station licensed to serve Kalispell, Montana. Since Kalispell is a city in Montana, the state where KOFI is located is Montana.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Montana', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To answer the original question about the busiest airport that shares a state with KOFI, I first need to determine which state KOFI is associated with. Once that state is identified, the next logical step is to find the busiest airport in that state. Since the current sub-question asks about the busiest airport in Montana, it assumes that KOFI is located in Montana, and thus this sub-question is a necessary step toward identifying the correct airport.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'What is the busiest airport in Montana?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "Bozeman Yellowstone International Airport is the busiest airport in the state of Montana, surpassing Billings Logan International Airport in the spring of 2013. Montana's other major airports include Billings Logan International Airport, Missoula International Airport, Great Falls International Airport, Glacier Park International Airport, Helena Regional Airport, Bert Mooney Airport and Yellowstone Airport. Eight smaller communities have airports designated for commercial service under the Essential Air Service program.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context states that Bozeman Yellowstone International Airport is the busiest airport in the state of Montana, surpassing Billings Logan International Airport in 2013. Therefore, the answer is Bozeman Yellowstone International Airport.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Bozeman Yellowstone International Airport', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks for the busiest airport that shares a state with KOFI. First, we determine the state where KOFI is located, which is Montana. Next, we identify the busiest airport in Montana, which is Bozeman Yellowstone International Airport. Therefore, the answer is Bozeman Yellowstone International Airport.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'Bozeman Yellowstone International Airport', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 953, 'user': 'When did the owner of Izze change from sugar to corn syrup?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', "The original question asks about the year the owner of Izze changed from using sugar to corn syrup. To determine this, I first need to identify who currently owns Izze, as the ownership change would be tied to the company's history.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Who owns Izze?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Izze (pronounced iz-ee) is the brand name of a line of carbonated juice drinks produced by the IZZE Beverage Company in Boulder, Colorado, which is owned by PepsiCo. The drinks consist of 70% fruit juice from concentrate, and 30% seltzer water. Izze does not contain added preservatives.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The answer is formed by identifying the company that owns the IZZE Beverage Company, as stated in the context. The text explicitly mentions that the IZZE Beverage Company is owned by PepsiCo. Therefore, the owner of Izze is PepsiCo.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'PepsiCo', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the date when the owner of Izze switched from sugar to corn syrup. Since Izze is owned by PepsiCo, understanding when PepsiCo made this change is essential to answering the original question. This sub-question narrows the focus to the company that owns Izze, allowing us to trace the change in sweetener usage.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'When did PepsiCo change from using sugar to corn syrup?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "The Pepsi - Cola Made with Real Sugar, formerly called Throwback, is a brand of soft drink sold by PepsiCo in the United States and in sweet stores in South Australia for its flagship Pepsi and Mountain Dew brands. The drinks, called Pepsi Throwback and Mountain Dew Throwback, are named as such because they are flavored with cane sugar and beet sugar instead of high fructose corn syrup, which soft drink companies used to replace sugar (in their North American products) in the 1980s. In addition, these drinks use retro packaging. As of June 2014, Pepsi Throwback has been replaced in one area of the United States by ``Pepsi - Cola Made with Real Sugar '', a new product formulation, also made without high fructose corn syrup.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context explains that soft drink companies in North America started using high fructose corn syrup to replace sugar in the 1980s. This indicates that the shift from sugar to corn syrup occurred during that decade. Therefore, the answer is "the 1980s.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'the 1980s', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The final answer is determined by first identifying the owner of Izze, which is PepsiCo. Then, by finding out when PepsiCo switched from using sugar to corn syrup, we determine that this change occurred in the 1980s. Thus, the answer is the 1980s.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'the 1980s', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 3168, 'user': 'When was the city where Deirdre McCloskey was born founded?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'To answer the original question about when the city where Deirdre McCloskey was born was founded, I first need to determine the specific city where she was born. This sub-question is the starting point in the reasoning chain, as identifying the birthplace is essential before we can investigate the founding date of that city.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Where was Deirdre McCloskey born?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Deirdre Nansen McCloskey (born September 11, 1942 in Ann Arbor, Michigan), is the Distinguished Professor of Economics, History, English, and Communication at the University of Illinois at Chicago (UIC). She is also adjunct professor of Philosophy and Classics there, and for five years was a visiting Professor of philosophy at Erasmus University, Rotterdam. Since October 2007 she has received six honorary doctorates. In 2013, she received the Julian L. Simon Memorial Award from the Competitive Enterprise Institute for her work examining factors in history that led to advancement in human achievement and prosperity. Her main research interests include the origins of the modern world, the misuse of statistical significance in economics and other sciences, and the study of capitalism, among many others.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'To determine where Deirdre McCloskey was born, we look for information in the context that directly states her place of birth. The context mentions, "Deirdre Nansen McCloskey (born September 11, 1942 in Ann Arbor, Michigan)." This clearly identifies Ann Arbor, Michigan as her birthplace. Therefore, the answer is Ann Arbor.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Ann Arbor', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To answer the original question about when the city where Deirdre McCloskey was born was founded, I first need to determine which city she was born in. Once that city is identified, the next step is to find out its founding date. Since the current sub-question asks about Ann Arbor, it is likely the city of her birth, and we now need to find its founding year.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'When was Ann Arbor founded?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "Ann Arbor was founded in 1824, named for wives of the village's founders and the stands of Bur Oak trees. The University of Michigan moved from Detroit to Ann Arbor in 1837, and the city grew at a rapid rate in the early to mid-20th century. During the 1960s and 1970s, the city gained a reputation as a center for left-wing politics. Ann Arbor became a focal point for political activism and served as a hub for the civil-rights movement and anti-Vietnam War movement, as well as various student movements.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'Ann Arbor was founded in 1824, as stated directly in the context. The answer is formed by identifying the specific year mentioned in the first sentence of the context, which provides the founding date of the city.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', '1824', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks for the founding year of the city where Deirdre McCloskey was born. First, we determine the city of birth by answering the subquery "Where was Deirdre McCloskey born?" which gives the answer "Ann Arbor." Next, we find the founding year of Ann Arbor by answering the subquery "When was Ann Arbor founded?" which provides the answer "1824." Combining these results, the final answer is 1824.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', '1824', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 1098, 'user': "When did Louis Deniset's political party form?", 'assistant': ['<step>\n', "To answer the original question about when Louis Deniset's political party formed, I first need to identify which political party he was associated with. This is necessary because the formation date of the party is directly tied to the party's name, and without knowing the specific party, it is impossible to determine the correct formation year.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Which political party was Louis Deniset a member of?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Louis Deniset (June 29, 1919 – August 26, 1983) was a Liberal Party of Canada member for Saint Boniface, Manitoba, from October 14, 1957, to February 1, 1958.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'Louis Deniset was a member of the Liberal Party of Canada, as stated in the context, which explicitly mentions that he was a Liberal Party of Canada member for Saint Boniface, Manitoba. Therefore, the answer is directly derived from the information provided in the context.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Liberal Party of Canada', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', "The original question asks about the formation year of Louis Deniset's political party. To answer this, I first need to determine which political party Louis Deniset was associated with, and since he was a Canadian politician, the next logical step is to investigate the formation date of the Liberal Party of Canada, which is the party he was known to be part of.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'When was the Liberal Party of Canada formed?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'The Liberals are descended from the mid-19th century Reformers who agitated for responsible government throughout British North America. These included George Brown, Robert Baldwin, William Lyon Mackenzie and the Clear Grits in Upper Canada, Joseph Howe in Nova Scotia, and the Patriotes and Rouges in Lower Canada led by figures such as Louis - Joseph Papineau. The Clear Grits and Parti rouge sometimes functioned as a united bloc in the legislature of the Province of Canada beginning in 1854, and a united Liberal Party combining both English and French Canadian members was formed in 1861.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context states that a united Liberal Party combining both English and French Canadian members was formed in 1861. This directly answers the question by providing the specific year the Liberal Party of Canada was formed.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', '1861', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', "To determine when Louis Deniset's political party formed, first identify the political party he was a member of, which is the Liberal Party of Canada. Then, find the formation year of that party, which is 1861. Therefore, the final answer is 1861.", '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', '1861', '</answer>\n']}
