{'id': 1147, 'user': 'The 88000 model of the company that invented the first mobile phone was a type of what?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the type of the 88000 model from the company that invented the first mobile phone. To determine this, I first need to identify which company invented the first mobile phone, as this will allow me to find the relevant model and its classification.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Who invented the first mobile phone?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Prior to 1973, mobile telephony was limited to phones installed in cars and other vehicles. Motorola was the first company to produce a handheld mobile phone. On April 3, 1973, Martin Cooper, a Motorola researcher and executive, made the first mobile telephone call from handheld subscriber equipment, placing a call to Dr. Joel S. Engel of Bell Labs, his rival. The prototype handheld phone used by Dr. Cooper weighed 1.1 kilograms (2.4 lb) and measured 23 by 13 by 4.5 centimetres (9.1 by 5.1 by 1.8 in). The prototype offered a talk time of just 30 minutes and took 10 hours to re-charge.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context states that Motorola was the first company to produce a handheld mobile phone and that Martin Cooper made the first mobile telephone call using a prototype from Motorola. Therefore, the answer "Motorola" refers to the company that invented the first mobile phone.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Motorola', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the type of architecture of the 88000 model, which is associated with the company that invented the first mobile phone. To answer this, I first need to identify the company that invented the first mobile phone, and then determine what type of architecture the 88000 model represents. The current sub-question focuses on the architecture of the 88000 model, which is a necessary step in answering the original question.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'What type of architecture was the 88000 model?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'The 88000 (m88k for short) is a RISC instruction set architecture (ISA) developed by Motorola during the 1980s. The 88000 arrived on the market in 1988, some two years after the competing SPARC and MIPS. Due to the late start and extensive delays releasing the second-generation MC88110, the m88k achieved very limited success outside of the MVME platform and embedded controller environments. When Motorola joined the AIM alliance in 1991 to develop the PowerPC, further development of the 88000 ended.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The question asks for the type of architecture of the 88000 model. The context states that the 88000 is a "RISC instruction set architecture (ISA)" developed by Motorola. Therefore, the answer "ISA" is directly derived from the definition provided in the context.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'ISA', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the type of the 88000 model from the company that invented the first mobile phone. First, we identify the company as Motorola, based on the subquery answer. Then, we determine that the 88000 model was based on ISA architecture. Combining these two pieces of information, the final answer is ISA.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'ISA', '</answer>\n']}
