 associated with Rod Jones, the next step is to find out who the quarterback was on that team during their Super Bowl win.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Who was the quarterback on the Tampa Bay Buccaneers when they won the Super Bowl?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "The Raiders had a great chance to score a touchdown early in the game after cornerback Charles Woodson intercepted Buccaneers quarterback Brad Johnson's pass on the third play of the game and returned it 12 yards to the Tampa Bay 36 - yard line. However, six plays later, Tampa Bay defensive end Simeon Rice sacked Raiders quarterback Rich Gannon on third down, forcing Oakland to settle for kicker Sebastian Janikowski's 40 - yard field goal to give them a 3 -- 0 lead.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context mentions that Brad Johnson was the quarterback for the Buccaneers when he was intercepted by Charles Woodson. This directly identifies Brad Johnson as the quarterback on the Tampa Bay Buccaneers at the time they won the Super Bowl, as the scenario described is from a game involving the Buccaneers. Therefore, the answer is Brad Johnson.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Brad Johnson', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', "To determine the quarterback on Rod Jones' team when they won the Super Bowl, first identify the team Rod Jones played for, which is the Tampa Bay Buccaneers. Then, find out who was the quarterback for the Buccaneers during their Super Bowl victory. The quarterback was Brad Johnson. Therefore, the final answer is Brad Johnson.", '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'Brad Johnson', '</answer>\n']}
