s the Czech Republic.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Czech Republic', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', "The final answer is determined by first identifying Jiří Kejval's birthplace, which is Prague. Then, it is established that the Embassy of Sweden in Prague is located in the Czech Republic. Therefore, the country where the Embassy of Sweden can be found in Jiří Kejval's birthplace is the Czech Republic.", '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'Czech Republic', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 10661, 'user': 'What is the main source of electricity in the province where Eric Robinson was Deputy Premier?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The main question asks for the main source of electricity in the province where Eric Robinson was Deputy Premier. To answer this, I first need to determine which specific province Eric Robinson served as Deputy Premier in.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'In which province was Eric Robinson Deputy Premier?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'The Deputy Premier is a cabinet minister in the province of Manitoba, Canada. The position has existed for several years, but only appears to have become a full-fledged cabinet portfolio in 1988. Between 2009 and 2011, the position was held by both Eric Robinson and Rosann Wowchuk. The current Deputy Premier is Heather Stefanson under Premier Brian Pallister.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'In the context, it is stated that Eric Robinson held the position of Deputy Premier in the province of Manitoba, Canada. The text explicitly mentions that the Deputy Premier is a cabinet minister in Manitoba, and it specifically notes that Eric Robinson served in this role between 2009 and 2011. Therefore, the answer is Manitoba.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Manitoba', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', "To answer the original question, I first need to determine which province Eric Robinson was Deputy Premier in. Once that province is identified, the next step is to find out the main source of electricity in that specific province. Since the current sub-question focuses on Manitoba, it is a necessary step to gather the relevant information about Manitoba's electricity source.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'What is the main source of electricity in Manitoba?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Manitoba Hydro is the electric power and natural gas utility in the province of Manitoba, Canada. Founded in 1961, it is a provincial Crown Corporation, governed by the Manitoba Hydro - Electric Board and the Manitoba Hydro Act. Today the company operates 15 interconnected generating stations. It has more than 527,000 electric power customers and more than 263,000 natural gas customers. Since most of the electrical energy is provided by hydroelectric power, the utility has low electricity rates. Stations in Northern Manitoba are connected by a HVDC system, the Nelson River Bipole, to customers in the south. The internal staff are members of the Canadian Union of Public Employees Local 998 while the outside workers are members of the International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers Local 2034.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', "Manitoba Hydro is the electric power and natural gas utility in Manitoba, and it operates the majority of the province's generating stations. Since the context states that most of the electrical energy is provided by hydroelectric power, and Manitoba Hydro is the main provider of electricity in the province, the answer is Manitoba Hydro.", '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Manitoba Hydro', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To determine the main source of electricity in the province where Eric Robinson was Deputy Premier, first identify the province by asking "In which province was Eric Robinson Deputy Premier?" The answer is Manitoba. Next, find the main source of electricity in Manitoba by asking "What is the main source of electricity in Manitoba?" The answer is Manitoba Hydro. Therefore, the main source of electricity in that province is Manitoba Hydro.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'Manitoba Hydro', '</answer>\n']}
