{'id': 8515, 'user': 'when did the currencies of the country where Tete is located first come into circulation?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the year when the currencies of the country where Tete is located first came into circulation. To answer this, I first need to determine which country Tete is located in, as the currency information will depend on that specific nation.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'In which country is Tete located?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Tete is the capital city of Tete Province in Mozambique. It is located on the Zambezi River, and is the site of two of the four bridges crossing the river in Mozambique. A Swahili trade center before the Portuguese colonial era, Tete continues to dominate the west-central part of the country and region, and is the largest city on the Zambezi. In the local language, Nyungwe, Tete (or Mitete) means "reed."', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'Tete is mentioned as the capital city of Tete Province in the context. The text explicitly states that Tete is located in Mozambique. Therefore, the answer is Mozambique.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Mozambique', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the introduction of the currencies of the country where Tete is located. To answer this, I first need to identify which country Tete is in, and since Tete is a city in Mozambique, the next step is to determine when the currencies of Mozambique first came into circulation.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'When did the currencies of Mozambique first come into circulation?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'The metical (MZM) replaced the escudo at par on 16 June 1980. It was divided into 100 centavos. The metical underwent severe inflation. After the revaluation of the Romanian leu, the metical briefly became the least valued currency unit, at a value of about 24,500 meticais per USD, until the Zimbabwean dollar took the title in late August 2005.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The answer is formed by identifying the key date in the context when the metical (MZM) replaced the escudo. The context states that this replacement occurred "on 16 June 1980," which directly answers the question about when the currencies of Mozambique first came into circulation.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', '16 June 1980', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To form the final answer, first determine the country where Tete is located, which is Mozambique. Then, find out when the currencies of Mozambique first came into circulation, which is 16 June 1980. Therefore, the final answer is 16 June 1980.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', '16 June 1980', '</answer>\n']}
