on Apple's post-desktop sales growth to address the original question.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', "After the failure of Apple's desktop sales, what products drove their sales growth?", '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "Starting in 2002, Apple moved to eliminate CRT displays from its product line as part of aesthetic design and space-saving measures with the iMac G4. However, the new iMac with its flexible LCD flat-panel monitor was considerably more expensive on its debut than the preceding iMac G3, largely due to the higher cost of the LCD technology at the time. In order to keep the Macintosh affordable for the education market and due to obsolescence of the iMac G3, Apple created the eMac in April 2002 as the intended successor; however the eMac's CRT made it relatively bulky and somewhat outdated, while its all-in-one construction meant it could not be expanded to meet consumer demand for larger monitors. The iMac G4's relatively high prices were approaching that of laptops which were portable and had higher resolution LCD screens. Meanwhile, Windows PC manufacturers could offer desktop configurations with LCD flat panel monitors at prices comparable to the eMac and at much lower cost than the iMac G4. The flop of the Power Mac G4 Cube, along with the more expensive iMac G4 and heavy eMac, meant that Macintosh desktop sales never reached the market share attained by the previous iMac G3. For the next half-decade while Macintosh sales held steady, it would instead be the iPod portable music player and iTunes music download service that would drive Apple's sales growth.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', "The context explains that after the failure of Apple's desktop sales, the company's sales growth was driven by two products: the iPod portable music player and the iTunes music download service. This is directly stated in the final sentence of the context, which highlights that these products were the ones that drove Apple's sales growth during the period when desktop sales were stagnant.", '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'the iPod portable music player and
{'id': 12417, 'user': 'The father of Katti Anker Møller was a citizen of what country?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', "The original question asks about the country of citizenship of Katti Anker Møller's father. To determine this, I first need to identify who her father is, as the country of citizenship will depend on the individual's background.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Who is the father of Katti Anker Møller?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'She was born Cathrine Anker in Hamar, the daughter of Herman Anker. She had nine siblings and grew up around the first folk high school at Sagatun in Hamar, which was founded by her father. Educated as a teacher, she spent a year in France, where her exposure to the life of prostitutes and single mothers affected her profoundly. Her mother died at the age of 50, apparently exhausted from her many pregnancies though the number of children she had was normal for her time.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context states that Katti Anker Møller was born Cathrine Anker, the daughter of Herman Anker. This directly identifies Herman Anker as her father. Therefore, the answer is Herman Anker.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Herman Anker', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', "The original question asks about the country of citizenship of Katti Anker Møller's father. To answer this, I first need to identify who Katti Anker Møller's father is, which leads to the sub-question about Herman Anker's country of citizenship.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'What country was Herman Anker a citizen of?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'The first of its kind in Norway, it was founded by Herman Anker and Olaus Arvesen in 1864. The school building was erected around 1865, and drawn by architect Emil Victor Langlet. The school was disestablished in 1892, having been headed by Arvesen from 1873 to 1878 and 1880 to 1892.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'To determine the country Herman Anker was a citizen of, we look at the context provided. The text mentions that Herman Anker founded a school in Norway in 1864, along with Olaus Arvesen. Since the school was established in Norway and the context refers to events taking place there, it indicates that Herman Anker was a citizen of Norway.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Norway', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To determine the country of citizenship of Herman Anker, the father of Katti Anker Møller, we first identify Herman Anker as the father. Then, we find that Herman Anker was a citizen of Norway. Therefore, the answer is Norway.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'Norway', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 4775, 'user': 'When did Flatline by the One Less Lonely Girl singer come out?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The main question asks for the release year of the song "Flatline" by the singer of "One Less Lonely Girl." To determine this, I first need to identify who the singer of "One Less Lonely Girl" is, as that will allow me to find the correct artist and subsequently the release date of their song "Flatline.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', "Who is the singer of 'One Less Lonely Girl'?", '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', '"One Less Lonely Girl" is a song by Canadian recording artist Justin Bieber. The song was written and produced by Bieber\'s mentor, Usher, as well as Ezekiel Lewis, Balewa Muhammad of The Clutch, and A-Rex duo Sean Hamilton and Hyuk Shin. It was released exclusively to iTunes as the second single from his debut release, "My World" on October 6, 2009, and was later released to more digital distributions and mainstream and rhythmic radio soon after.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', '1. The question asks for the singer of the song "One Less Lonely Girl."  \n2. The context explicitly states that the song is by Canadian recording artist Justin Bieber.  \n3. Therefore, the answer is Justin Bieber.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Justin Bieber', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To answer the original question about when "Flatline" by the One Less Lonely Girl singer came out, I first need to identify which artist is referred to by the nickname "One Less Lonely Girl." Once that is determined, the next step is to find out the release date of the song "Flatline" by that artist.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', "When did 'Flatline' by Justin Bieber come out?", '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "On December 9, 2013, Bieber announced that the ten Music Monday releases would be packaged with an additional five new songs in a compilation entitled Complete My Journals. Although the album was initially set for release on December 16, 2013, the date was pushed back one week to December 23, as Bieber intended to include one more song on the compilation. Though it does not appear on the album itself, the bonus track, ``Flatline '', was available for a free download on the iTunes Store for a limited time. Journals was available on iTunes from January 2, 2014, and all sixteen songs are available for purchase individually. According to one of its producers and Bieber's personal friend, Jason`` Poo Bear'' Boyd, the album was supposed to receive a full release, as well as its singles to be promoted on radio, however the label did n't support it because it was n't the direction they wanted Justin to go. It was, however, eventually released on LP in 2016.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'Flatline was released as a bonus track on the compilation album "Complete My Journals," which was available on iTunes starting on January 2, 2014. Therefore, the answer is January 2, 2014.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'January 2, 2014', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks for the release date of "Flatline" by the singer of "One Less Lonely Girl." First, we identify the singer of "One Less Lonely Girl," which is Justin Bieber. Next, we determine the release date of "Flatline" by Justin Bieber, which is January 2, 2014. Therefore, the final answer is January 2, 2014.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'January 2, 2014', '</answer>\n']}
