{'id': 502, 'user': 'Who is the mother of the last Democratic presidential candidate to win any counties in Oklahoma?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', "The original question asks for the mother of the last Democratic presidential candidate to win any counties in Oklahoma. To answer this, I first need to identify who that specific candidate was, as the mother's identity depends on knowing the candidate's name.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Who was the last Democratic presidential candidate to win any counties in Oklahoma?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "After the 1948 election, the state turned firmly Republican. Although registered Republicans were a minority in the state until 2015, starting in 1952, Oklahoma has been carried by Republican presidential candidates in all but one election (1964). This is not to say that every election has been a landslide for Republicans: Jimmy Carter lost the state by less than 1.5% in 1976, while Michael Dukakis and Bill Clinton both won 40% or more of the state's popular vote in 1988 and 1996 respectively. Al Gore in 2000, though, was the last Democrat to even win any counties in the state. Oklahoma was the only state where Barack Obama failed to carry any of its counties in both 2008 and 2012.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'the answer is formed by identifying the last Democratic presidential candidate who won any counties in Oklahoma. The context states that "Al Gore in 2000, though, was the last Democrat to even win any counties in the state." This directly answers the question by specifying Al Gore as the last Democratic candidate to achieve this.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Al Gore', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To answer the original question, I first need to identify the last Democratic presidential candidate to win any counties in Oklahoma. Al Gore is known to have won counties in Oklahoma during his 2000 presidential campaign. Therefore, the next step is to determine who his mother is, which will help answer the original question.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Who is the mother of Al Gore?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Pauline LaFon Gore (October 6, 1912 – December 15, 2004) was the mother of former United States Vice President Al Gore and the wife of former United States Senator Al Gore Sr.. She is credited with playing a significant role in both of their careers with Al Gore saying "there will never be a better campaigner than Pauline LaFon Gore". Her advice was an important factor in his refusal to sign the "Southern Manifesto" opposing desegregation and his opposition to the Vietnam War which were critical issues in his bid for re-election as a Senator in 1970. She came from a poor family in small business to become one of the first female lawyers to graduate from Vanderbilt University and managed a Washington law firm in the 1970s.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', "The context directly states that Pauline LaFon Gore was the mother of Al Gore. By identifying this information from the text, the answer is formed by simply extracting the name of Al Gore's mother as provided in the context.", '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Pauline LaFon Gore', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The final answer is determined by first identifying the last Democratic presidential candidate to win any counties in Oklahoma, which is Al Gore. Then, by finding the mother of Al Gore, we arrive at the final answer: Pauline LaFon Gore.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'Pauline LaFon Gore', '</answer>\n']}
