dentify the county where that city serves as the seat of government. The current sub-question focuses on finding the county that is the seat of Knoxville, which is a key step in locating the city associated with Neyland Stadium.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Which county is the seat of Knoxville?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'The Knoxville City-County Building is a building at 400 Main Street in Knoxville, Tennessee that houses the offices of the city government of Knoxville and the county government of Knox County, Tennessee. It also houses the Knox County Jail. The building stands ten stories, and contains of office space. At the time it was built it was said to be the largest office building in Tennessee.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The answer is determined by identifying the county associated with the Knoxville City-County Building, which is explicitly stated in the context as the building that houses the offices of the county government of Knox County, Tennessee. Therefore, the county with the seat of Knoxville is Knox County.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Knox County', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The city where Neyland Stadium is located is Knoxville. The county that serves as the seat of Knoxville is Knox County. Therefore, the final answer is Knox County.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'Knox County', '</answer>\n']}
