ment in 1934 to centralize federal record keeping, with the Archivist of the United States as chief administrator. The National Archives was incorporated with GSA in 1949; in 1985 it became an independent agency as NARA (National Archives and Records Administration).', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'NARA became an independent agency in 1985, as stated in the context. The text explicitly mentions that "in 1985 it became an independent agency as NARA (National Archives and Records Administration)." This directly answers the question by providing the specific year when NARA achieved independence.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', '1985', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks for the year the agency responsible for maintaining the Presidential Library system became independent. First, we identify the agency, which is NARA. Then, we determine the year NARA became an independent agency, which is 1985. Therefore, the final answer is 1985.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', '1985', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 2680, 'user': 'When did the torch arrive in the city Songyo-guyok is located?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The main question asks about the arrival year of the torch in the city where Songyo-guyok is located. To answer this, I first need to determine the specific city in which Songyo-guyok is situated.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'In which city is Songyo-guyok located?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "Sŏn'gyo-guyŏk or Songyo District is one of the 19 guyŏk that constitute the city of Pyongyang, North Korea. It is on the eastern bank of the Taedong River at the center of East Pyongyang. It is bordered to the south by Nakrang-guyok, to the north by Tongdaewon-guyok and to the east by Ryokpo and Sadong-guyoks. It was established in September 1959.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context states that Songyo-guyok is one of the 19 guyŏk that make up the city of Pyongyang. Therefore, the answer is derived directly from this information, identifying Pyongyang as the city in which Songyo-guyok is located.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Pyongyang', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To answer the original question about when the torch arrived in the city where Songyo-guyok is located, I first need to determine which city Songyo-guyok is in. Since the sub-question asks about the arrival of the torch in Pyongyang, it is likely that Songyo-guyok is located in Pyongyang, and this sub-question is the first step in identifying the city to proceed with the original question.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'When did the torch arrive in Pyongyang?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "North Korea: The event was held in Pyongyang on April 28. It was the first time that the Olympic torch has traveled to North Korea. A crowd of thousands waving pink paper flowers and small flags with the Beijing Olympics logo were organized by the authoritarian regime watched the beginning of the relay in Pyongyang, some waving Chinese flags. The event was presided over by the head of the country's parliament, Kim Yong Nam. The North, an ally of China, has been critical of disruptions to the torch relay elsewhere and has supported Beijing in its actions against protests in Tibet. Kim passed the torch to the first runner Pak Du Ik, who played on North Korea's 1966 World Cup soccer team, as he began the 19-kilometre route through Pyongyang. The relay began from the large sculpted flame of the obelisk of the Juche Tower, which commemorates the national ideology of Juche, or 'self-reliance', created by the country's late founding President Kim Il Sung, father of leader Kim Jong Il, who did not attend.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'Now, I will generate the thought process for the given input:\n\nThe question asks for the date when the torch arrived in Pyongyang. The context mentions that the event was held in Pyongyang on April 28. This directly answers the question. Therefore, the answer is April 28.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'April 28', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To determine when the torch arrived in the city where Songyo-guyok is located, first identify the city: Songyo-guyok is located in Pyongyang. Next, find out when the torch arrived in Pyongyang. Based on the subanswers, the torch arrived in Pyongyang on April 28. Therefore, the final answer is April 28.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'April 28', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 2383, 'user': 'What sea washes on the shores of the birthplace of Jim Wilson?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The main question asks about the sea that washes on the shores of the birthplace of Jim Wilson. To answer this, I first need to determine where Jim Wilson was born, as that will identify the specific location and subsequently the sea associated with it.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Where was Jim Wilson born?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Born in County Antrim, Wilson attended Belfast College of Technology before becoming a marine engineer. He was elected to Newtownabbey Borough Council in 1975 for the Vanguard Unionist Progressive Party, and joined the Ulster Unionist Party the following year. However, he resigned his position on the council in 1988. He was UUP General Secretary from the late 1980s until 1998.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'To determine where Jim Wilson was born, we look for information in the context about his birthplace. The context states, "Born in County Antrim," which directly answers the question. Therefore, the answer is County Antrim.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'County Antrim', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', "The main question asks about the sea that washes on the shores of the birthplace of Jim Wilson. To answer this, I first need to determine where Jim Wilson was born. Since the birthplace is not directly provided, identifying a relevant location is necessary. County Antrim is a likely candidate for Jim Wilson's birthplace, so the next step is to find out which sea washes on its shores.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Which sea washes on the shores of County Antrim?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "In ancient times, Antrim was inhabited by a Celtic people called the Darini. In the early Middle Ages, southern County Antrim was part of the Kingdom of Ulidia, ruled by the Dál Fiatach clans Keenan and MacDonlevy/McDunlavey; the north was part of Dál Riada, which stretched into what is now western Scotland over the Irish Sea. Dál Riada was ruled by the O'Lynch clan, who were vassals of the Ulidians. Besides the Ulidians and Dál Riada, there were the Dál nAraide of lower County Antrim, and the Cruthin, who were pre-Gaelic Celts and probably related to the Picts of Britain. Between the 8th and 11th centuries Antrim was exposed to the inroads of the Vikings.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context mentions that Dál Riada, a region in northern County Antrim, stretched into what is now western Scotland over the Irish Sea. This indicates that the Irish Sea borders County Antrim. Therefore, the answer is Irish Sea.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Irish Sea', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The birthplace of Jim Wilson is County Antrim. The sea that washes on the shores of County Antrim is the Irish Sea. Therefore, the final answer is the Irish Sea.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'Irish Sea', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 16687, 'user': "When did the Black Death occur in the continent where the first leg of Queen's mid 2000s tour was, with the performer of Electric?", 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the occurrence of the Black Death on the continent where the first leg of Queen\'s mid-2000s tour took place, specifically mentioning the performer of the song "Electric." To answer this, I first need to identify who performed "Electric," as this will help determine which tour and, consequently, which continent is being referenced. This sub-question is the starting point in establishing the necessary context to locate the continent and then determine the timeline of the Black Death.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Who is the performer of Electric?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Electric (fully as Paul Rodgers Electric according to Paul Rodgers official site) is a studio album by Paul Rodgers of Free and Bad Company fame. It was recorded in 1999 at Lartington Hall Studios near Barnard Castle in the North East of England. Electric was released in 2000 (the Japanese version of 1999 has a bonus track).', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'Electric is a studio album mentioned in the context, and the text states that it is "by Paul Rodgers of Free and Bad Company fame." This directly identifies Paul Rodgers as the performer of the album Electric. Therefore, the answer is Paul Rodgers.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Paul Rodgers', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', "The original question asks about the occurrence of the Black Death on the continent where the first leg of Queen's mid-2000s tour with Paul Rodgers took place. To answer this, I first need to determine the location of that tour leg, as it will identify the relevant continent for the Black Death's timeline.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', "Where was the first leg of Queen's mid 2000s tour with Paul Rodgers?", '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "Between 2005 and 2006, Queen + Paul Rodgers embarked on a world tour, which was the first time Queen toured since their last tour with Freddie Mercury in 1986. The band's drummer Roger Taylor commented; 'We never thought we would tour again, Paul [Rodgers] came along by chance and we seemed to have a chemistry. Paul is just such a great singer. He's not trying to be Freddie.' The first leg was in Europe, the second in Japan, and the third in the US in 2006. Queen received the inaugural VH1 Rock Honors at the Mandalay Bay Events Center in Las Vegas, Nevada, on 25 May 2006. The Foo Fighters paid homage to the band in performing 'Tie Your Mother Down' to open the ceremony before being joined on stage by May, Taylor, and Paul Rodgers, who played a selection of Queen hits.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'Queen + Paul Rodgers embarked on a world tour between 2005 and 2006. The context explicitly states that the first leg of the tour was in Europe, followed by Japan and the US. Therefore, the answer is Europe.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Europe', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the occurrence of the Black Death in a specific continent, which is tied to the location of the first leg of Queen\'s mid 2000s tour involving the performer of "Electric." To answer this, I first need to determine which continent is associated with that tour leg. Since the next sub-question focuses on the Black Death in Europe, it assumes that the tour leg in question took place in Europe. This sub-question is a necessary step to establish the geographical context required to answer the original question.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'When did the Black Death occur in Europe?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'The Black Death was one of the most devastating pandemics in human history, resulting in the deaths of an estimated 75 to 200 million people in Eurasia and peaking in Europe from 1346 to 1353. The bacterium Yersinia pestis, resulting in several forms of plague, is believed to have been the cause. The plague created a series of religious, social, and economic upheavals, which had profound effects on the c
{'id': 12447, 'user': 'What is the minimum age to buy a handgun in the state where Glick-Sower House is located?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the minimum age to buy a handgun in the state where the Glick-Sower House is located. To answer this, I first need to determine which state the Glick-Sower House is located in, as different states have different laws regarding handgun purchase ages.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'In which state is the Glick-Sower House located?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'The Glick–Sower House, also known as the Susie Sower House, is located in Marshalltown, Iowa. The house was built in 1859 for Dr. George Glick and has been listed on the National Register of Historic Places since 1993. It is operated as a historic house museum by the Historical Society of Marshall County.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'In the context, it is stated that the Glick-Sower House is located in Marshalltown, Iowa. Therefore, the answer is Iowa, as the question asks for the state where the house is located.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Iowa', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the minimum age to buy a handgun in the state where Glick-Sower House is located. To answer this, I first need to determine which state Glick-Sower House is in. Once that is established, the next step is to find the minimum age requirement for purchasing a handgun in that specific state, which in this case is Iowa.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'What is the minimum age to buy a handgun in Iowa?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "A Permit To Acquire (PTA), obtained from the sheriff of the county of the applicant's residence, is required when purchasing or otherwise acquiring a handgun, either from a dealer or from a private party. A Permit To Acquire shall be issued to qualified applicants aged 21 or older. The PTA becomes valid three days after the date of application, and is valid for one year. A PTA is not required when purchasing an antique handgun, defined as one made in or before 1898 and including post-1898 replicas of matchlock, flintlock, or percussion cap pistols.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'To determine the minimum age to buy a handgun in Iowa, we look at the context provided. It states that a Permit To Acquire (PTA) is required for purchasing a handgun, and this permit is issued to "qualified applicants aged 21 or older." This directly indicates that the minimum age to obtain a PTA, and therefore to legally purchase a handgun, is 21 or older. Thus, the answer is "21 or older.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', '21 or older.', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The final answer is determined by first identifying the state where the Glick-Sower House is located, which is Iowa. Then, the minimum age to buy a handgun in Iowa is retrieved, which is 21 or older. Thus, the answer is 21 or older.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', '21 or older.', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 19740, 'user': 'What is the number of executive branch senators where the director of The Man from Morocco was born?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The original question asks for the number of executive branch senators where the director of *The Man from Morocco* was born. To answer this, I first need to identify who directed the film, as that information is essential to determine the birthplace of the director and subsequently find the number of executive branch senators from that region.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Who directed The Man from Morocco?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'The Man from Morocco is a 1945 action adventure film directed by Mutz Greenbaum as Max Greene. The film was produced by Welwyn Studios in Great Britain.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context states that "The Man from Morocco is a 1945 action adventure film directed by Mutz Greenbaum as Max Greene." From this, we can directly identify that Mutz Greenbaum was the director of the film. Therefore, the answer is Mutz Greenbaum.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Mutz Greenbaum', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', "The main question asks for the number of executive branch senators where the director of *The Man from Morocco* was born. To answer this, I first need to determine the birthplace of the film's director, Mutz Greenbaum, as this will identify the location associated with the number of executive branch senators.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Where was Mutz Greenbaum born?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Mutz Greenbaum (3 February 1896 – 5 July 1968), sometimes credited as Max Greene or Max Greenbaum, was a Berlin, Germany-born film cinematographer.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', '**Thought Process:**  \nThe question asks for the birthplace of Mutz Greenbaum. The context states that he was "Berlin, Germany-born," which directly answers the question. Therefore, the answer is Berlin.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Berlin', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To answer the original question, I first need to determine the number of executive branch senators in Berlin, as this will provide the context necessary to understand the structure of the executive branch senate in that city. This sub-question is the first step in identifying the relevant data needed to answer the original question.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'How many people are in the executive branch senate in Berlin?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "The governments in Berlin, Bremen and Hamburg are designated by the term Senate. In the three free states of Bavaria, Saxony, and Thuringia the government is referred to as the State Government (Staatsregierung), and in the other ten states the term Land Government (Landesregierung) is used. Before January 1, 2000, Bavaria had a bicameral parliament, with a popularly elected Landtag, and a Senate made up of representatives of the state's major social and economic groups. The Senate was abolished following a referendum in 1998. The states of Berlin, Bremen, and Hamburg are governed slightly differently from the other states. In each of those cities, the executive branch consists of a Senate of approximately eight, selected by the state's parliament; the senators carry out duties equivalent to those of the ministers in the larger states. The equivalent of the Minister-President is the Senatspräsident (President of the Senate) in Bremen, the Erster Bürgermeister (First Mayor) in Hamburg, and the Regierender Bürgermeister (Governing Mayor) in Berlin. The parliament for Berlin is called the Abgeordnetenhaus (House of Representatives), while Bremen and Hamburg both have a Bürgerschaft. The parliaments in the remaining 13 states are referred to as Landtag (State Parliament).", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', "The context explains that in Berlin, the executive branch consists of a Senate of approximately eight members, selected by the state's parliament. The question asks for the number of people in the executive branch senate in Berlin, so the answer is directly derived from this information.", '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n'
{'id': 6602, 'user': "How many national female outdoor track and field championships have been won by Allan Wicker's alma mater?", 'assistant': ['<step>\n', "The original question asks how many national female outdoor track and field championships have been won by Allan Wicker's alma mater. To determine this, I first need to identify which university Allan Wicker attended, as the alma mater is the institution associated with his athletic achievements.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Where did Allan Wicker attend university?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Allan W. Wicker (born 1941) studied with the founders of ecological psychology, Roger G. Barker and Herbert F. Wright, in the social psychology program at the University of Kansas, where he earned the Ph.D. in 1967. He taught at the University of Wisconsin, Milwaukee and the University of Illinois, Champaign-Urbana before taking a position at Claremont Graduate School (now Claremont Graduate University) in 1971, where he was a professor of psychology until early retirement in 1999. He is currently an emeritus professor.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'To determine where Allan Wicker attended university, we look for information in the context about his educational background. The context states that he "studied with the founders of ecological psychology, Roger G. Barker and Herbert F. Wright, in the social psychology program at the University of Kansas, where he earned the Ph.D. in 1967." This directly indicates that he attended the University of Kansas. Therefore, the answer is the University of Kansas.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'University of Kansas', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', "# Thought Process\n\nThe original question asks how many national female outdoor track and field championships have been won by Allan Wicker's alma mater. To answer this, I first need to determine which university Allan Wicker attended. Once that is known, the next step is to find out how many national championships that university has won in the specified sport. Therefore, the current sub-question is focused on identifying the number of championships won by the University of Kansas, which is likely Allan Wicker's alma mater, in order to answer the original question.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'How many national female outdoor track and field championships has the University of Kansas won?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "The school's sports teams, wearing crimson and royal blue, are called the Kansas Jayhawks. They participate in the NCAA's Division I and in the Big 12 Conference. KU has won thirteen National Championships: five in men's basketball (two Helms Foundation championships and three NCAA championships), three in men's indoor track and field, three in men's outdoor track and field, one in men's cross country and one in women's outdoor track and field. The home course for KU Cross Country is Rim Rock Farm. Their most recent championship came on June 8, 2013 when the KU women's track and field team won the NCAA outdoor in Eugene, Oregon becoming the first University of Kansas women's team to win a national title.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'University of Kansas has won one national female outdoor track and field championship, as stated in the context: "one in women\'s outdoor track and field." The answer is directly provided in the text.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'one', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', "To determine how many national female outdoor track and field championships have been won by Allan Wicker's alma mater, first identify the university he attended, which is the University of Kansas. Then, find out how many national female outdoor track and field championships the University of Kansas has won. Based on the subanswers, the final answer is one.", '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'one', '</answer>\n']}
