{'id': 5984, 'user': 'When was the developer of Taddei Tondo born?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', "Original question: When was the developer of Taddei Tondo born?\n\nThe main question asks for the birth year of the person who developed Taddei Tondo. To determine this, I first need to identify who the developer of Taddei Tondo is. Once the developer's identity is established, I can then proceed to find their birth year.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Who developed Taddei Tondo?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "The Taddei Tondo or The Virgin and Child with the Infant St John is a marble relief tondo (circular composition) by Italian Renaissance artist Michelangelo Buonarroti. Part of the permanent collection of the Royal Academy of Arts in London, it is the only marble sculpture by Michelangelo in Great Britain. A 'perfect demonstration' of his carving technique, the work delivers a 'powerful emotional and narrative punch.'", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context states that the Taddei Tondo is a marble relief tondo by Michelangelo Buonarroti. This directly identifies Michelangelo as the artist who developed the work. Therefore, the answer is Michelangelo.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Michelangelo', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'Now that I know the developer of Taddei Tondo is Michelangelo, the next step is to find out when Michelangelo was born in order to answer the original question.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'When was Michelangelo born?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "Michelangelo was born on 6 March 1475 in Caprese, known today as Caprese Michelangelo, a small town situated in Valtiberina, near Arezzo, Tuscany. For several generations, his family had been small-scale bankers in Florence; but the bank failed, and his father, Ludovico di Leonardo Buonarroti Simoni, briefly took a government post in Caprese, where Michelangelo was born. At the time of Michelangelo's birth, his father was the town's Judicial administrator and podestà or local administrator of Chiusi della Verna. Michelangelo's mother was Francesca di Neri del Miniato di Siena. The Buonarrotis claimed to descend from the Countess Mathilde of Canossa—a claim that remains unproven, but which Michelangelo believed. Several months after Michelangelo's birth, the family returned to Florence, where he was raised. During his mother's later prolonged illness, and after her death in 1481 (when he was six years old), Michelangelo lived with a nanny and her husband, a stonecutter, in the town of Settignano, where his father owned a marble quarry and a small farm. There he gained his love for marble. As Giorgio Vasari quotes him:", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'To determine Michelangelo\'s birth date, we look for specific information in the context. The text states, "Michelangelo was born on 6 March 1475 in Caprese," which directly provides the answer. Therefore, the answer is 6 March 1475.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', '6 March 1475', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'inal answer is formed by first identifying the developer of Taddei Tondo, which is Michelangelo. Then, determining the birth date of Michelangelo, which is 6 March 1475. Combining these two pieces of information gives the final answer.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', '6 March 1475', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 1027, 'user': 'When did the man who said "I came; I saw; I conquered" die?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The original question asks for the death date of the man who said "I came; I saw; I conquered." To determine this, I first need to identify who made that famous statement, as the next step will involve finding the death date of that individual.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', "Who said 'I came; I saw; I conquered'?", '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "``Veni, vidi, vici'' (Classical Latin: (ˈweːniː ˈwiːdiː ˈwiːkiː); Ecclesiastical Latin: (ˈvɛni ˈvidi ˈvitʃi);) ``I came; I saw; I conquered'' is a Latin phrase popularly attributed to Julius Caesar who, according to Appian, used the phrase in a letter to the Roman Senate around 47 BC after he had achieved a quick victory in his short war against Pharnaces II of Pontus at the Battle of Zela. The phrase is used to refer to a swift, conclusive victory.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The answer is formed by identifying the person associated with the Latin phrase "Veni, vidi, vici," which translates to "I came; I saw; I conquered." The context explicitly states that the phrase is "popularly attributed to Julius Caesar," confirming that he is the speaker of the quote. Thus, the answer is Julius Caesar.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Julius Caesar', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the death date of the man who said "I came; I saw; I conquered," which is a well-known quote attributed to Julius Caesar. To answer this, the first step is to identify who that man was. Once it is established that the quote belongs to Julius Caesar, the next sub-question logically follows: determining when he died. This sub-question is essential to directly address the original question.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'When did Julius Caesar die?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "Caesar was now the primary figure of the Roman state, enforcing and entrenching his powers. His enemies feared that he had ambitions to become an autocratic ruler. Arguing that the Roman Republic was in danger, a group of senators hatched a conspiracy and assassinated Caesar at a meeting of the Senate in March 44 BC. Mark Antony, Caesar's lieutenant, condemned Caesar's assassination, and war broke out between the two factions. Antony was denounced as a public enemy, and Caesar's adopted son and chosen heir, Gaius Octavianus, was entrusted with the command of the war against him. At the Battle of Mutina Mark Antony was defeated by the consuls Hirtius and Pansa, who were both killed.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'the context states that Caesar was assassinated in March 44 BC by a group of senators who feared his ambitions. The answer is directly derived from this specific date mentioned in the text.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'March 44 BC', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To determine when the man who said "I came; I saw; I conquered" died, we first identify who made that statement. The subquery "Who said \'I came; I saw; I conquered\'?" yields the answer "Julius Caesar." Next, we find the date of Julius Caesar\'s death by answering the subquery "When did Julius Caesar die?" which gives "March 44 BC." Therefore, the final answer is March 44 BC.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'March 44 BC', '</answer>\n']}
