 and Italy completed?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'The unification of Germany into a politically and administratively integrated nation state officially occurred on 18 January 1871, in the Hall of Mirrors at the Palace of Versailles in France. Princes of the German states, excluding Austria, gathered there to proclaim Wilhelm I of Prussia as German Emperor after the French capitulation in the Franco - Prussian War. Unofficially, the de facto transition of most of the German - speaking populations into a federated organization of states had been developing for some time through alliances formal and informal between princely rulers -- but in fits and starts; self - interests of the various parties hampered the process over nearly a century of autocratic experimentation, beginning in the era of the Napoleonic Wars, which saw the dissolution of the Holy Roman Empire of the German Nation (1806), and the subsequent rise of German nationalism.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The answer is formed by identifying the specific date mentioned in the context when the unification of Germany was officially completed. The text states that the unification "officially occurred on 18 January 1871," which directly answers the question.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', '18 January 1871', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks for the date when Italy and the country that scored the most points in FIFA 2018 were unified into two countries. First, we determined that the country which scored the most points in FIFA 2018 was Germany. Next, we identified the date when the unification of Germany and Italy was completed, which is 18 January 1871. Therefore, the final answer is 18 January 1871.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', '18 January 1871', '</answer>\n']}
