nal question, we would need to first identify the specific U.S. location where the tank battalion was stationed, and then determine who initiated the 1934 general strike in that location.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Who initiated the general strike of 1934 in the U.S. location where the tank battalion was located?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "The 1934 West Coast Waterfront Strike (also known as the 1934 West Coast Longshoremen's Strike, as well as a number of variations on these names) lasted eighty-three days, and began on May 9, 1934 when longshoremen in every West Coast port walked out. The strike peaked with ``Bloody Thursday'' and the San Francisco General Strike which stopped all work in the major port city for four days and led ultimately to the settlement of the West Coast Longshoremen's Strike.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The question asks who initiated the general strike of 1934 in the U.S. location where the tank battalion was located. The context mentions the 1934 West Coast Waterfront Strike, which began when longshoremen in every West Coast port walked out. Although the context does not explicitly mention a tank battalion, the answer refers to the longshoremen as the initiators of the strike. Therefore, the answer identifies the longshoremen as the ones who initiated the strike.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'longshoremen in every West Coast port', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The final answer is determined by first identifying the location of the tank battalion, which is San Francisco. Then, using that location, the question is answered by identifying the group that initiated the general strike of 1934 in that area, which is the longshoremen in every West Coast port.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'longshoremen in every West Coast port', '</answer>\n']}
