{'id': 1134, 'user': 'In what season of American Idol was the performer of My Love a guest judge?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the season of *American Idol* in which the performer of "My Love" was a guest judge. To determine this, I first need to identify who the performer of the song "My Love" is, as that will allow me to find out which *American Idol* season they appeared as a guest judge.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', "Who is the performer of 'My Love'?", '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', '"My Love" is the title of a 1983 hit song by the American singer-songwriter Lionel Richie. It was the third single released off Richie\'s self-titled debut solo album. The song features harmony backing vocals by country music singer Kenny Rogers. It reached the Top 10 on three notable "Billboard" magazine charts in the spring of 1983: on the pop chart, the song peaked at # 5; on the adult contemporary chart, the song spent four weeks at # 1; and on the R&B chart, the song topped out at # 6. "My Love" was not among Richie\'s more successful singles in the United Kingdom, where it only managed # 70 on the UK Singles Chart. In Canada it peaked on the RPM Singles chart at #28.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'My Love" is a 1983 hit song by Lionel Richie, as stated in the context. The answer is directly provided in the context, identifying Lionel Richie as the performer of the song.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Lionel Richie', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The main question asks about the season of *American Idol* in which the performer of "My Love" was a guest judge. Since "My Love" is a song by Lionel Richie, the next step is to determine in which season of *American Idol* Lionel Richie served as a guest judge. This sub-question directly identifies the key figure mentioned in the original question and sets the stage for finding the correct season.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'In which season of American Idol was Lionel Richie a guest judge?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Guest judges may occasionally be introduced. In season two, guest judges such as Lionel Richie and Robin Gibb were used, and in season three Donna Summer, Quentin Tarantino and some of the mentors also joined as judges to critique the performances in the final rounds. Guest judges were used in the audition rounds for seasons four, six, nine, and fourteen such as Gene Simmons and LL Cool J in season four, Jewel and Olivia Newton-John in season six, Shania Twain in season eight, Neil Patrick Harris, Avril Lavigne and Katy Perry in season nine, and season eight runner-up, Adam Lambert, in season fourteen.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'In the context, it is stated that Lionel Richie was a guest judge in season two of American Idol. The text explicitly mentions that in season two, guest judges such as Lionel Richie and Robin Gibb were used. Therefore, the answer is season two.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'season two', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To determine the season of American Idol in which the performer of "My Love" was a guest judge, first identify the performer of the song "My Love," which is Lionel Richie. Next, find out in which season of American Idol Lionel Richie served as a guest judge, which is season two. Therefore, the final answer is season two.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'season two', '</answer>\n']}
