{'id': 13471, 'user': "When did the locale for that's so raven stop minting circulating coins?", 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the year when the locale for "That\'s So Raven" stopped minting circulating coins. To answer this, I first need to identify which specific locale the show is set in, as the concept of "minting circulating coins" is typically associated with a geographic or fictional location that has a currency or monetary system. Therefore, determining the locale of the show is the necessary first step.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', "In which locale does 'That's So Raven' take place?", '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "The show was set in San Francisco and revolved around teenager Raven Baxter, played by Raven - Symoné, her friends Eddie (Orlando Brown) and Chelsea (Anneliese van der Pol), her family members; mother Tanya Baxter (T'Keyah Crystal Keymáh), father Victor Baxter (Rondell Sheridan) and brother Cory (Kyle Massey). The title character drew on her psychic powers, ingenuity, and talent as a fashion designer as well as a variety of disguises to get into and out of amusing adolescent and pre-adolescent situations.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context states that the show "That\'s So Raven" was set in San Francisco. This directly answers the question about the locale of the show. Therefore, the answer is San Francisco.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'San Francisco', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question refers to "that\'s so raven," which is a nickname for the San Francisco Mint. To determine when the locale associated with this nickname stopped minting circulating coins, the first step is to identify which specific mint is being referred to. Once confirmed as the San Francisco Mint, the next step is to find out when it ceased circulating coin production.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'When did the San Francisco Mint stop minting circulating coins?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'The San Francisco Mint is a branch of the United States Mint and was opened in 1854 to serve the gold mines of the California Gold Rush. It quickly outgrew its first building and moved into a new one in 1874. This building, the Old United States Mint, also known affectionately as The Granite Lady, is one of the few that survived the great 1906 San Francisco earthquake. It served until 1937, when the present facility was opened.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The answer is formed by identifying the key information in the context about when the San Francisco Mint stopped minting circulating coins. The context states that the Old United States Mint building served until 1937, when the present facility was opened. This indicates that the San Francisco Mint stopped minting circulating coins in 1937.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', '1937', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks when the locale for "That\'s So Raven" stopped minting circulating coins. First, we determine the locale where the show takes place, which is San Francisco. Next, we find out when the San Francisco Mint stopped minting circulating coins, which is 1937. Therefore, the final answer is 1937.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', '1937', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 7551, 'user': 'What is the mosaic in the church where Villa Bianca is located known as?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', "The original question asks about the name of the mosaic in the church where Villa Bianca is located. To determine this, I first need to identify the location of Villa Bianca, as the mosaic's name is tied to the specific church in that location.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Where is Villa Bianca located?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Villa Bianca or Villa Fernandez is the name of a famous mansion in the city of Thessaloniki, Greece. It is located in Vassilisis Olgas street and was built between 1911 und 1913 as a residence for Dino Fernandez Diaz and his family. The architect was Pietro Arrigoni (variously also spelled: Piero/Pierro Arigon/Arrigon/Arigoni).', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'You are asked to determine the location of Villa Bianca. The context states that Villa Bianca is a famous mansion in the city of Thessaloniki, Greece. From this information, it is clear that the answer is Thessaloniki, as the city is explicitly mentioned as the location of the villa.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Thessaloniki', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The main question asks for the name of the mosaic in the church where Villa Bianca is located. To answer this, I first need to determine which church in Thessaloniki is associated with Villa Bianca, as the mosaic in question is located there.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'What is the name of the mosaic in the church located in Thessaloniki?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "Very few early Byzantine mosaics survived the Iconoclastic destruction of the 8th century. Among the rare examples are the 6th-century Christ in majesty (or Ezekiel's Vision) mosaic in the apse of the Church of Hosios David in Thessaloniki that was hidden behind mortar during those dangerous times. Nine mosaic panels in the Hagios Demetrios Church, which were made between 634 and 730, also escaped destruction. Unusually almost all represent Saint Demetrios of Thessaloniki, often with suppliants before him.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', "The context mentions that the 6th-century Christ in majesty (or Ezekiel's Vision) mosaic is located in the apse of the Church of Hosios David in Thessaloniki. This directly answers the question by identifying the name of the mosaic in the church located in Thessaloniki.", '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', "Christ in majesty (or Ezekiel's Vision)", '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks for the name of the mosaic in the church where Villa Bianca is located. First, we determine that Villa Bianca is located in Thessaloniki. Next, we identify the name of the mosaic in the church located in Thessaloniki, which is "Christ in majesty (or Ezekiel\'s Vision)." Therefore, the final answer is "Christ in majesty (or Ezekiel\'s Vision).', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', "Christ in majesty (or Ezekiel's Vision)", '</answer>\n']}
