Katy Perry as a guest judge?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Guest judges may occasionally be introduced. In season two, guest judges such as Lionel Richie and Robin Gibb were used, and in season three Donna Summer, Quentin Tarantino and some of the mentors also joined as judges to critique the performances in the final rounds. Guest judges were used in the audition rounds for seasons four, six, nine, and fourteen such as Gene Simmons and LL Cool J in season four, Jewel and Olivia Newton-John in season six, Shania Twain in season eight, Neil Patrick Harris, Avril Lavigne and Katy Perry in season nine, and season eight runner-up, Adam Lambert, in season fourteen.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context mentions that Katy Perry was a guest judge in season nine, specifically noting that in season nine, guest judges included Neil Patrick Harris, Avril Lavigne, and Katy Perry. Therefore, the answer is season nine.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'season nine', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The lyricist of the song "Peacock" is Katy Perry. The season of American Idol that featured Katy Perry as a guest judge is season nine. Therefore, the final answer is season nine.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'season nine', '</answer>\n']}
