{'id': 6352, 'user': "When was Commander-in-Chief in JAKAZiD's city of birth abolished?", 'assistant': ['<step>\n', "The original question asks about the year the position of Commander-in-Chief was abolished in the city where JAKAZiD was born. To answer this, I first need to determine the city of JAKAZiD's birth, as this is the specific location where the abolition of the position is being asked.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Where was JAKAZiD born?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Joshua James "Josh" McInnes (born May 7, 1988), better known by his artist name JAKAZiD, is a record producer from Portsmouth, England. He owns and manages the label Aural Adrenaline and was previously signed to the record label Nukleuz. He is usually associated with writing happy hardcore music and remixing other well-known songs in this style.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'To determine where JAKAZiD was born, we look at the context provided. The text states that Joshua James "Josh" McInnes, known as JAKAZiD, is a record producer from Portsmouth, England. The phrase "from Portsmouth, England" indicates his place of birth. Therefore, the answer is Portsmouth.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Portsmouth', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To answer the original question about when the Commander-in-Chief position in JAKAZiD\'s city of birth was abolished, I first need to identify the city where JAKAZiD was born. Since the original question refers to "JAKAZiD\'s city of birth," the next logical step is to determine which city that is. If it is known or can be inferred that JAKAZiD was born in Portsmouth, then the sub-question about the abolition of the Commander-in-Chief position in Portsmouth becomes relevant to answering the original question.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'When was the Commander-in-Chief position in Portsmouth abolished?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'The post of Commander-in-Chief, Portsmouth was merged with that of Commander-in-Chief, Plymouth in 1969 to form the post of Commander-in-Chief, Naval Home Command. The posts of Second Sea Lord and Commander-in-Chief Naval Home Command were amalgamated in 1994 following the rationalisation of the British Armed Forces following the end of the Cold War. In 2012, however, all distinct Commander-in-Chief appointments were discontinued, with full operational command being vested instead in the First Sea Lord; he now flies his flag from HMS "Victory".', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', "Now, let's break down how to form the answer based on the context. The question asks when the Commander-in-Chief position in Portsmouth was abolished. The context explains that the post of Commander-in-Chief, Portsmouth was merged with that of Commander-in-Chief, Plymouth in 1969 to form the post of Commander-in-Chief, Naval Home Command. This indicates that the position in Portsmouth was abolished in 1969 when the merger occurred. Therefore, the answer is 1969.", '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', '1969', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To form the final answer, first determine the city where JAKAZiD was born, which is Portsmouth. Then, find out when the Commander-in-Chief position in Portsmouth was abolished, which is 1969. Therefore, the final answer is 1969.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', '1969', '</answer>\n']}
