ill be to find historical records of Australian military activity in that area.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'When did Australian troops fight in New Britain, Connecticut?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Initial fighting on New Britain took place around the western end of the island in December 1943 and January 1944, with US forces landing and securing bases around Arawe and Cape Gloucester. This was followed by a further landing in March 1944 around Talasea, after which little fighting took place between the ground forces on the island. In October 1944, Australian forces took over from the US troops and undertook a Landing at Jacquinot Bay the following month, before beginning a limited offensive to secure a defensive line across the island between Wide Bay and Open Bay behind which they contained the numerically greatly superior Japanese forces for the remainder of the war. The Japanese regarded the New Britain Campaign as a delaying action, and kept their forces concentrated around Rabaul in expectation of a ground assault which never came.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The answer is formed by identifying the specific time when Australian troops were involved in the New Britain campaign. The context states that in October 1944, Australian forces took over from the US troops and undertook a landing at Jacquinot Bay. This directly answers the question by providing the month and year when Australian troops fought in New Britain, Connecticut.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'October 1944', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', "To determine when Australian troops fought in the area where Stag Arms's headquarters is located, first identify the location of Stag Arms's headquarters, which is New Britain, Connecticut. Next, find the date when Australian troops fought in New Britain, Connecticut. Based on the subanswers, the final answer is October 1944.", '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'October 1944', '</answer>\n']}
