{'id': 11521, 'user': 'Where are the San Juan mountains located in the state where Tsankawi is located?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', "To answer the original question, I first need to determine the state where Tsankawi is located, as the San Juan Mountains' location depends on that information.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'In which state is Tsankawi located?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Tsankawi is a detached portion of Bandelier National Monument in New Mexico, near White Rock. It is accessible from a roadside parking area just north of the intersection of East Jemez Road and State Road 4. A self-guided 1.5-mile loop trail provides access to numerous unexcavated ruins, caves carved into soft tuff, and petroglyphs. A trail guide, available at the entrance, provides a detailed description of the area.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'Now, I need to determine the state where Tsankawi is located. The context states that Tsankawi is a part of Bandelier National Monument in New Mexico. This directly identifies the state as New Mexico. Therefore, the answer is New Mexico.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'New Mexico', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the location of the San Juan Mountains within the state where Tsankawi is located. To answer this, I first need to determine which state Tsankawi is in. Once that is established, the next step is to identify where the San Juan Mountains are located within that specific state, which is New Mexico.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Where are the San Juan Mountains located in New Mexico?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'The San Juan Mountains are a high and rugged mountain range in the Rocky Mountains in southwestern Colorado and northwestern New Mexico. The area is highly mineralized (the Colorado Mineral Belt) and figured in the gold and silver mining industry of early Colorado. Major towns, all old mining camps, include Creede, Lake City, Silverton, Ouray, and Telluride. Large scale mining has ended in the region, although independent prospectors still work claims throughout the range. The last large scale mines were the Sunnyside Mine near Silverton, which operated until late in the 20th century and the Idarado Mine on Red Mountain Pass that closed down in the 1970s. Famous old San Juan mines include the Camp Bird and Smuggler Union mines, both located between Telluride and Ouray.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The San Juan Mountains are described in the context as being located in "southwestern Colorado and northwestern New Mexico." The question specifically asks about their location in New Mexico, so the answer focuses on the "northwestern" part of New Mexico where the mountains extend.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'northwestern New Mexico', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To form the final answer, first determine the state where Tsankawi is located, which is New Mexico. Then, identify where the San Juan Mountains are located within that state, which is northwestern New Mexico. Combining these two pieces of information gives the final answer: northwestern New Mexico.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'northwestern New Mexico', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 4292, 'user': 'What college did the current quarterback of the team that once included Alex Espinoza attend?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', "The original question asks about the college attended by the current quarterback of the team that once included Alex Espinoza. To determine this, I first need to identify which sports team Alex Espinoza played for, as this will help establish the team's history and allow me to trace the current quarterback's college affiliation.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Which sports team did Alex Espinoza play for?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Alex A. Espinoza (born May 31, 1964) is a former National Football League quarterback who played for one season with the Kansas City Chiefs. He went to college at Iowa State after transferring from Cal State-Fullerton. During the strike shortened season of 1987 he was picked up as an undrafted free agent to serve as a backup quarterback by Kansas City and played in only one game. He compiled 69 yards on 9 out of 14 attempts with two interceptions and five rushing yards in his lone NFL game, a 42–0 loss at Miami in his lone NFL year.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context states that Alex Espinoza played for the Kansas City Chiefs in the National Football League. It specifically mentions that he was picked up by the Kansas City Chiefs as a backup quarterback and played in one game. Therefore, the answer is Kansas City Chiefs.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Kansas City Chiefs', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the college attended by the current quarterback of the team that once included Alex Espinoza. To answer this, I first need to identify which team currently includes Alex Espinoza, and then determine the current quarterback of that team. Since Alex Espinoza was a player for the Kansas City Chiefs, the next step is to find out where the current quarterback of the Kansas City Chiefs attended college.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Where did the quarterback of the Kansas City Chiefs attend college?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Patrick Lavon Mahomes II (born September 17, 1995) is an American football quarterback for the Kansas City Chiefs of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football at Texas Tech, and was drafted by the Chiefs with the tenth overall pick in the 2017 NFL Draft. Mahomes is the son of former MLB pitcher Pat Mahomes.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The answer is formed by identifying the relevant information in the context. The context states that Patrick Mahomes, the quarterback of the Kansas City Chiefs, "played college football at Texas Tech." This directly answers the question about where the quarterback attended college. Therefore, the answer is "Texas Tech.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Texas Tech', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The current quarterback of the Kansas City Chiefs, who is the same team that once included Alex Espinoza, attended college at Texas Tech. Therefore, the final answer is Texas Tech.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'Texas Tech', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 6215, 'user': 'Since 1994, who has been in charge of the city the Turkish Angora is named after?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the person in charge of the city that the Turkish Angora is named after since 1994. To answer this, I first need to identify which city the Turkish Angora is named after, as this is the foundational piece of information required to proceed.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Which city is the Turkish Angora named after?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "The Turkish Angora (, 'Ankara cat') is a breed of a domestic cat. Turkish Angoras are one of the ancient, natural breeds of cat, having originated in central Turkey, in the Ankara region. The breed has been documented as early as the 17th century and is believed to be the origin of the mutations for both the coloration white and long hair. The breed is also sometimes referred to as simply the Angora or Ankara cat.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The answer is formed by identifying the key information in the context. The context states that the Turkish Angora originated in central Turkey, specifically in the Ankara region. The breed is also referred to as the "Ankara cat," which directly indicates that the city it is named after is Ankara.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Ankara', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks about the person in charge of the city the Turkish Angora is named after, which is Ankara. To answer this, I first need to identify the city associated with the Turkish Angora, which is Ankara. Now that I know the city is Ankara, the next step is to determine who has been in charge of Ankara since 1994.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Who has been in charge of Ankara since 1994?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "Melih Gökçek has been the Metropolitan Mayor of Ankara since 1994 as a politician from the Welfare Party. He later joined the Virtue Party and then the AKP. Initially elected in the 1994 local elections, he was re-elected in 1999, 2004 and 2009. In the 2014 local election, Gökçek stood for a fifth term. The MHP metropolitan mayoral candidate for the 2009 local elections, conservative politician Mansur Yavaş, stood as the CHP candidate against Gökçek. In a heavily controversial election, Gökçek was declared the winner by just 1% ahead of Yavaş amid allegations of systematic electoral fraud. With the Supreme Electoral Council and courts rejecting Yavaş's appeals, he has declared intention to take the irregularities to the European Court of Human Rights. Although Gökçek was inaugurated for a fifth term, most election observers believe that Yavaş was the winner of the election.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context states that Melih Gökçek has been the Metropolitan Mayor of Ankara since 1994. This directly answers the question, confirming that he has been in charge of Ankara since 1994.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Melih Gökçek', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'To form the final answer, first determine the city the Turkish Angora is named after, which is Ankara. Then, identify who has been in charge of Ankara since 1994, which is Melih Gökçek. Therefore, the final answer is Melih Gökçek.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'Melih Gökçek', '</answer>\n']}
