dividual rocks.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'James Dwight Dana died in New Haven, Connecticut, as indicated by the context, which states that the Dana House is located at 24 Hillhouse Avenue in New Haven, Connecticut, and was the home of James Dwight Dana. Since the house was his residence and he died in the 19th century, it is reasonable to conclude that he died in New Haven.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'New Haven', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The main question asks for the county whose capital is the city where the person the Danalites were named after died. To proceed, I first need to determine the capital of the county where New Haven is located, as this will help identify the relevant county and, eventually, the person associated with the Danalites.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'What is the capital of the county where New Haven is located?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'North Haven is a town in New Haven County, Connecticut on the outskirts of New Haven, Connecticut. As of the 2010 census, it had a population of 24,093.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'You need to determine the capital of the county where New Haven is located. The context states that New Haven is in New Haven County, Connecticut. Therefore, the county in question is New Haven County. Since the question asks for the capital of that county, the answer is simply the name of the county, as it is the capital of itself.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'New Haven County', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The final answer is determined by first identifying that the Danalites were named after James Dwight Dana. Next, it is found that James Dwight Dana died in New Haven. Finally, it is determined that New Haven is located in New Haven County, making New Haven County the answer.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'New Haven County', '</answer>\n']}
{'id': 5135, 'user': "When did the performer of the M+M's Tour release her first album?", 'assistant': ['<step>\n', "The original question asks about the release year of the first album by the performer of the M+M's Tour. To determine this, I first need to identify who the performer of the M+M's Tour was, as that information is essential for finding the release date of their first album.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', "Who was the performer of the M+M's Tour?", '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'The M+M\'s Tour was the sixth concert tour by American recording artist Britney Spears, consisting of six brief shows at clubs in the United States. Spears expressed interest in touring again as early as February 2006. She started rehearsing for a show at House of Blues venues in secret, and pulled out of a surprise performance on April 25, 2007, at Los Angeles nightclub Forty Deuce. After a marquee reading "The M+M\'s" at the House of Blues in San Diego, California, appeared in late April 2007, media sources identified the act as Spears, and the show quickly sold out. The title, "M+M\'s" code name was claimed to be Mother (after having two children) and Miss (after being divorced). The tour marked the first time Spears performed live since The Onyx Hotel Tour in June 2004.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The answer can be determined by identifying the performer mentioned in the context. The text states that "The M+M\'s Tour was the sixth concert tour by American recording artist Britney Spears," which directly indicates that Britney Spears was the performer of the tour.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Britney Spears', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', "The original question asks about the release date of the first album by the performer of the M+M's Tour. To answer this, I first need to identify who the performer of the M+M's Tour is. Since it is widely known that Britney Spears was the performer of the M+M's Tour, the next step is to determine when she released her first album.", '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'When did Britney Spears release her first album?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "Britney Jean Spears (born December 2, 1981) is an American singer, dancer, and actress. Born in McComb, Mississippi, and raised in Kentwood, Louisiana, she performed acting roles in stage productions and television shows as a child before signing with Jive Records in 1997. Spears's first and second studio albums,... Baby One More Time (1999) and Oops!... I Did It Again (2000), became international successes, with the former becoming the best-selling album by a teenage solo artist. Title tracks ``... Baby One More Time ''and`` Oops!... I Did It Again'' broke international sales records. In 2001, Spears released her self-titled third studio album, Britney, and played the starring role in the film Crossroads (2002). She assumed creative control of her fourth studio album, In the Zone (2003), which yielded the worldwide success of the single ``Toxic ``.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'the answer is formed by identifying the release year of Britney Spears\'s first album. The context states that her first and second studio albums were "Baby One More Time" (1999) and "Oops!... I Did It Again" (2000). Therefore, the first album was released in 1999.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', '1999', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', "The performer of the M+M's Tour is Britney Spears. Britney Spears released her first album in 1999. Therefore, the answer is 1999.", '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', '1999', '</answer>\n']}
