{'id': 1793, 'user': 'Who was the QB of the team that won the NFL Super Bowl in 2003?', 'assistant': ['<step>\n', 'The original question asks for the quarterback (QB) of the team that won the NFL Super Bowl in 2003. To determine this, I first need to identify which team was the winner of that Super Bowl. Once the winning team is known, I can then find out who their quarterback was.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Which team won the NFL Super Bowl in 2003?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', 'Super Bowl XXXVII was an American football game between the American Football Conference (AFC) champion Oakland Raiders and the National Football Conference (NFC) champion Tampa Bay Buccaneers to decide the National Football League (NFL) champion for the 2002 season. The Buccaneers defeated the Raiders by the score of 48 -- 21, tied with Super Bowl XXXV for the seventh largest Super Bowl margin of victory, and winning their first ever Super Bowl. The game, played on January 26, 2003 at Qualcomm Stadium in San Diego, California, was the sixth Super Bowl to be held a week after the conference championship games (XVII, XXV, XXVIII, XXXIV, and XXXVI). It was also the last Super Bowl played in the month of January. Super Bowl XXXVI was the first to be played in February, due to the NFL postponing games for a week after the September 11 attacks. Starting with Super Bowl XXXVIII in 2004, the Super Bowl has been permanently played in February. This was the last Super Bowl until Super Bowl 50 to take place in California.', '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context states that Super Bowl XXXVII was played in 2003 and that the Tampa Bay Buccaneers defeated the Oakland Raiders. Therefore, the Tampa Bay Buccaneers won the NFL Super Bowl in 2003.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Tampa Bay Buccaneers', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The original question asks for the quarterback of the team that won the NFL Super Bowl in 2003. To determine this, I first need to identify which team won the Super Bowl in 2003. The Tampa Bay Buccaneers were the winners that year, so the next step is to find out who was their quarterback at that time.', '</step>\n', '<subquery>\n', 'Who was the quarterback of the Tampa Bay Buccaneers when they won the Super Bowl in 2003?', '</subquery>\n', '<retrieval>\n', "The Raiders had a great chance to score a touchdown early in the game after cornerback Charles Woodson intercepted Buccaneers quarterback Brad Johnson's pass on the third play of the game and returned it 12 yards to the Tampa Bay 36 - yard line. However, six plays later, Tampa Bay defensive end Simeon Rice sacked Raiders quarterback Rich Gannon on third down, forcing Oakland to settle for kicker Sebastian Janikowski's 40 - yard field goal to give them a 3 -- 0 lead.", '</retrieval>\n', '<step>\n', 'The context mentions that Brad Johnson was the quarterback of the Tampa Bay Buccaneers during the game against the Raiders, where he threw an interception early in the game. Since the question asks for the quarterback of the Tampa Bay Buccaneers when they won the Super Bowl in 2003, and the context refers to a game involving the Buccaneers and their quarterback, Brad Johnson is identified as the correct answer.', '</step>\n', '<subanswer>\n', 'Brad Johnson', '</subanswer>\n', '<step>\n', 'The final answer is determined by first identifying the team that won the NFL Super Bowl in 2003, which is the Tampa Bay Buccaneers. Then, the quarterback of that team during their victory is identified as Brad Johnson. Therefore, the answer is Brad Johnson.', '</step>\n', '<answer>\n', 'Brad Johnson', '</answer>\n']}
